@tradition spice-shelf-supper
// Spice shelf supper (0.60.7): everyone brought one spice from home. Brennan cooks Tuesday dinner with three of them,
// and the jars line a shelf by the servery that grows over the weeks (the deck architect's spice shelf, always there).
// A meal tradition: going to it IS dinner for those who go.
k: 443
title: Spice shelf supper
when: weekly tuesday
at: 18:15-19:15
min: 25
where: 3 room Mess hall: mess-seat
hold: none
who: brennan always, lingers-at-meals 70%, galley 60%, everyone 40%
anim: talk
host: brennan
from: brennan
ties: galley meal=dinner
trace: spiceJars
meal: dinner


== mail
- Spice shelf supper tomorrow at {time}. I'm picking three jars from the shelf. Bring a guess, and an appetite.

== ask
- Spice shelf supper tonight. Brennan picked three jars. Guess whose.
- Supper's a mystery tonight. Three spices off the shelf.

== here
- That's mine! That warm one. That's from home.   #warm
- Is that smoky one yours? It's lovely.
- Brennan never says whose jar it is. We have to guess.

== thanks
- Brennan sets out supper made with three jars from the spice shelf, and the whole mess tries to guess whose they are.   #warm

== chatter
- Spice shelf supper tonight. Hope she picks my jar.
- That shelf's got half the galaxy on it now.   #warm
- Bring a spice from home next leave. Brennan will use it.
